  "schedule": "Sequential fresh worker processes; rotate the three main methods per case and round, alternate the additional controls. Five workers per case/method, each verifies bytes/SHA-256, warms, then measures three request batches. Same fixture files and exact Node 26.12.0. Small cases use Response.arrayBuffer; bulk cases drain to a counting Node writable. All methods include JSON generation and UTF-8 output. Normal Drizzle constructs a query per request, calls all(), JSON.stringify(), and encodes the full text. Source schema/column declaration and connection/Drizzle initialization are outside timing. Fixed 256-row table batching and 64 KiB buffering are unchanged. Both query-export controls use row streaming. The drizzle-host control imports Drizzle, declares the same schema and wraps the native connection, then calls direct ExportLite on that connection. Natural GC, no forced collection. Peak RSS is whole-worker high-water including imports, validation, warmup and timed requests. No ZIP, HTTP, disk output or remote latency."
}
